# Cloudflare Workers static assets honour this file (Pages and Netlify do too).
# Everything here is static; the only freshness that matters is the JSON snapshots.
#
# Verified against the live deployment: /*, /assets/*, /lib/*, /data/* and /*.md all take
# effect as written. The HTML is deliberately absent — Workers answers /index.html with a 307
# to /, so a rule keyed on /index.html can never match anything, and the default for / is
# already "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", which is what a page that ships new code wants
# anyway. The previous version had a /index.html rule that had never once applied.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/lib/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Refreshed by scripts/build-data.mjs — keep the window short.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/*.md
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
  Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8
